+## Challenge and independent review
+
+Root challenged the same-turn receipt wording, filtered/hidden boundaries, original artwork pixels, validation and failed saves, configuration persistence, and default Quit behaviour. Quit wording promises saved settings are kept instead of assuming its Dock icon remains after quitting; the final text was checked in the native confirmation. Native inspection exposed dense slider tick marks; the control is now continuous. Snapshot inspection caught unsupported AppKit TextField rendering and an accidental reload disabling loaded controls: snapshots use a read-only representation of that field, and the real view only starts loading when it has no settings. The running app's native editable field was checked separately.
+
+Separate reviewer agent `/root/ui8_review` initially found:
+
+1. Quit silently refused until all initial window requests succeeded. Fixed: independently bundled catalogue notes; tests exercise unloaded and failing window/popover, with the footer fallback included.
+2. Three fixtures marked Claude through turn4 while turn3 was waiting. Fixed: contiguous boundary turn2 and corresponding notes in status.d3_filled, status.d3_filled_3 and status.d4_s7. A Python test audits every status fixture's received prefix; the reviewer independently checked 43 boundaries.
+3. Reset continued after a generic failure if optional notes were absent, potentially reporting Saved. Fixed: write returns success independently of text; reset stops after the failed key. The no-notes regression records exactly theme/glass attempts and asserts failed/no Saved.
+
+Reviewer recheck: “UI8 recheck approved: all three findings are resolved, with focused regressions added. No remaining code-review blockers found.” Footer follow-up: “Approved. The footer fallback remains available before loading and after failure. Quit still reaches the application delegate’s confirmation gate.” Final gate results below were run by root after those repairs and the final visual changes.
+
+## Decisions and limits
+
+Ibrahim requested these visible changes. Orchestrator choices, checked by the independent reviewer: white silhouette edge in both menu appearances (dark wallpaper can occur in light macOS); existing receipt identity for grouping; saved fixture-only Settings slice now, remaining D11 setup later. Settings response notes are additive and optional; existing keys/defaults and marker protocol are unchanged. The settings transport omits plan flags while retaining the existing API parameter for compatibility. All new copy is in the catalogue; hand-made fixtures carry rendered notes until C2.
+
+The menu remains a 22-point mark, including a small I.A signature. PNG rendering/pixel checks cover its white edge, transparent margins and decision badge; no direct live system status-item photograph is claimed. Popover fixture rendering covers the compact footer, but direct status-item interaction was not separately photographed. Native app screenshots show Settings and the contrast/position of shared receipts. Quit confirmation and Return cancellation were exercised on the owned fixture, followed by a confirmed fixture restart. No other app was closed or reopened. The final executable matches the rebuilt source hash and the final app is open on Settings with Ibrahim's System choice retained; the tested notice toggle was restored to On.
+
+ImageRenderer's token-entry snapshot is a static representation of the native TextField; live native Settings inspection is the visual evidence for that editable control. Generated PNGs remain git-ignored under app/Snapshots. No new checkpoint result is claimed. Plain default Swift commands retain the recorded SDK27 macro-loading issue; the final gate uses installed SDK26.5 and its TestingMacros library as shown below.
